16
00:44.100 --> 00:45.340
I should go see him?

17
00:48.070 --> 00:48.550
Ow...

18
00:48.670 --> 00:49.340
Little Jam.

19
00:49.790 --> 00:50.690
Mr. Sarm?!

20
00:51.140 --> 00:51.850
- Let me go! - What are you doing?

21
00:51.880 --> 00:52.350
You can't.

22
00:52.350 --> 00:53.460
I haven't done anything wrong!

23
00:53.790 --> 00:54.290
I repeat!

24
00:54.760 --> 00:55.780
I love you!

25
00:55.900 --> 00:57.500
I love you every single second!

26
00:57.500 --> 00:59.520
I love you with every breath I take!

27
00:59.520 --> 01:00.290
Listen...

28
01:00.600 --> 01:01.490
I love you.

29
01:01.490 --> 01:02.190
What should we do with him?

30
01:02.190 --> 01:03.350
Take him away, Poj.

31
01:03.350 --> 01:03.890
Huh?!

32
01:03.890 --> 01:04.510
Come with us.

33
01:04.510 --> 01:05.090
- Huh? - Now!

34
01:05.340 --> 01:09.670
♫I've held back, but you're impossible to resist♫

35
01:09.690 --> 01:13.200
♫'Cause you make me wanna kiss, kiss♫

36
01:13.210 --> 01:17.820
♫Never thought I'd fall for you♫

37
01:17.820 --> 01:20.500
♫Accidentally gave you my heart♫

38
01:20.520 --> 01:23.990
♫Wanna be close to you, can you tell me if this is love?♫

39
01:24.010 --> 01:27.610
♫It feels so right, should I let my heart take control?♫

40
01:27.610 --> 01:30.900
♫You're too cute, you drive me crazy♫

41
01:30.920 --> 01:34.690
♫Just a glance from you almost melts me, baby♫

42
01:35.590 --> 01:37.890
♫Can I give a cutie like you a kiss?♫

43
01:37.900 --> 01:39.700
♫Can I give you one more kiss?♫

44
01:39.700 --> 01:41.740
♫You♫

45
01:41.740 --> 01:43.300
♫Just a bit more♫

46
01:43.300 --> 01:44.940
♫Can I kiss you one more time?♫

47
01:44.970 --> 01:46.830
♫Can I give you one more kiss?♫

48
01:46.830 --> 01:48.840
♫I'm not gonna lie♫

49
01:48.870 --> 01:50.500
♫If I can't kiss you now, I'd lose my mind♫

50
01:50.530 --> 01:54.030
♫You, ou, ou, ou♫

51
01:54.050 --> 01:57.539
♫You, ou, ou, ou, ou♫

52
01:57.560 --> 02:00.980
♫You, ou, ou, ou♫

53
02:01.000 --> 02:03.050
♫You, ou, ou, ou♫

54
02:03.070 --> 02:05.920
♫If I can't kiss you now, I'd lose my mind♫

55
02:05.940 --> 02:07.710
♫Everyone tells me to hold my horses♫

56
02:07.730 --> 02:09.470
♫But the sight of you bugs my system♫

57
02:09.490 --> 02:11.290
♫You in my heart, I won't miss my chance♫

58
02:11.310 --> 02:13.040
♫Aiming right at you, only you♫

59
02:13.060 --> 02:15.600
♫Six, five, four, three, two, one♫

60
02:15.630 --> 02:16.950
♫I'll count it down♫

61
02:16.970 --> 02:20.780
♫One more sec, and I'll kiss, kiss you, alright♫

62
02:20.800 --> 02:24.250
♫Wanna be close to you, can you tell me if this is love?♫

63
02:24.270 --> 02:27.920
♫You in my heart, I won't miss my chance♫

64
02:27.950 --> 02:31.320
♫You're too cute, you drive me crazy♫

65
02:31.340 --> 02:35.230
♫Just a glance from you almost melts me, baby♫

66
02:36.600 --> 02:41.700
[Your Third Series]

67
02:47.620 --> 02:48.760
Juju.

68
02:48.780 --> 02:50.460
Where are you running off to?

69
03:41.850 --> 03:42.520
Hey.

70
03:43.280 --> 03:43.970
Oh?

71
03:44.290 --> 03:45.850
Good morning...sir.

72
03:46.810 --> 03:47.490
Oh...

73
03:47.490 --> 03:49.150
You were the guy who came here last night.

74
03:49.150 --> 03:50.000
Good morning.

75
03:51.270 --> 03:52.730
I've come in peace today.

76
03:52.910 --> 03:54.240
I've got you a gift.

77
03:55.250 --> 03:56.650
I run an orange farm, you see.

78
03:57.290 --> 03:59.290
That's why I've got you a voucher.

79
03:59.900 --> 04:02.010
You can redeem it for any product,

80
04:02.010 --> 04:02.860
with no quantity limit,

81
04:03.010 --> 04:04.060
all year long.

82
04:05.120 --> 04:06.050
And here...

83
04:07.100 --> 04:08.030
A free vacation.

84
04:08.560 --> 04:10.570
Accommodation is available at the nature campground

85
04:10.570 --> 04:11.490
on my farm.

86
04:11.490 --> 04:12.460
Whoa...

87
04:12.600 --> 04:13.990
Is this from Adisuan Farm?

88
04:14.750 --> 04:17.000
My wife and kids have been wanting to visit the campground for years now,

89
04:17.000 --> 04:18.290
but it's always fully booked.

90
04:18.290 --> 04:19.240
It fills up so quickly.

91
04:19.920 --> 04:21.079
Take them. For you,

92
04:21.079 --> 04:23.260
I can give it my all.

93
04:27.030 --> 04:28.060
Are you sure this is a good idea?

94
04:28.770 --> 04:30.570
Do you have an ulterior motive here?

95
04:31.440 --> 04:32.390
Sir.

96
04:32.390 --> 04:33.600
How could you ask me such a question?

97
04:33.750 --> 04:35.840
I just want us to get along well

98
04:35.980 --> 04:36.960
because

99
04:37.659 --> 04:39.230
I'll be a resident here.

100
04:39.450 --> 04:39.790
Oh?

101
04:39.790 --> 04:41.480
You're going to purchase a house here?

102
04:41.870 --> 04:42.850
Indeed.

103
04:47.560 --> 04:48.460
Uh, sir.

104
04:48.460 --> 04:49.130
Excuse me.

105
04:49.490 --> 04:51.670
Which one is Mr. Jiranat's house?

106
04:53.090 --> 04:54.050
All of them, actually.

107
04:54.290 --> 04:56.030
Mr. Jiranat owns this residential project.

108
04:58.670 --> 04:59.930
This is nothing fancy.

109
04:59.930 --> 05:03.220
I'm just buying a house from my soon-to-be partner's residential project.

110
05:04.350 --> 05:05.970
I haven't introduced myself, actually.

111
05:06.520 --> 05:07.410
I'm...

112
05:07.430 --> 05:08.490
Sarm Traiphop.

113
05:08.860 --> 05:09.440
Right.

114
05:09.440 --> 05:10.530
Pleasure to meet you, sir.

115
05:10.530 --> 05:12.010
I'm Poj, a security guard.

116
05:12.200 --> 05:12.810
It's nice to meet you.

117
05:14.860 --> 05:16.520
I'm off to see Mr. Jam now.

118
05:16.620 --> 05:18.530
Today, I'm doing things properly.

119
05:18.550 --> 05:19.390
Don't worry.

120
05:19.510 --> 05:20.330
- Right. - Alright.

121
05:20.350 --> 05:21.330
- Go ahead. - Right.

122
05:25.830 --> 05:26.680
Little Jam.

123
05:33.120 --> 05:34.060
Little Jam...

124
05:39.470 --> 05:40.150
Little Jam...

125
05:44.120 --> 05:45.030
Little Jam!

126
05:47.090 --> 05:48.400
Is he alright?

127
05:52.450 --> 05:53.490
Little Jam!

128
06:16.060 --> 06:16.890
Little Jam...

129
06:17.390 --> 06:18.330
Is he fine?

130
06:44.640 --> 06:45.490
Need to change into flip-flops,

131
06:45.770 --> 06:46.860
or else I'll get scolded.

132
06:56.440 --> 06:57.640
The door isn't locked either.

133
06:58.950 --> 07:00.280
Why is he so careless about security?

134
07:06.930 --> 07:08.000
Mr. Sarm?

135
07:08.490 --> 07:09.840
How did you come in?

136
07:16.930 --> 07:18.120
Little Jam.

137
07:18.710 --> 07:19.480
I'm sorry.

138
07:22.060 --> 07:24.460
I just let myself in

139
07:24.570 --> 07:25.660
because this door

140
07:26.640 --> 07:27.730
wasn't locked.

141
07:28.770 --> 07:30.280
That wasn't my intention.

142
07:30.640 --> 07:31.660
Actually,

143
07:32.490 --> 07:34.060
I texted you earlier,

144
07:34.770 --> 07:35.700
but you didn't reply.

145
07:36.610 --> 07:37.159
I called you...

146
07:37.320 --> 07:38.520
but you didn't answer.

147
07:39.790 --> 07:40.890
So I got worried,

148
07:41.550 --> 07:42.960
thinking that something happened to you.

149
07:45.210 --> 07:46.580
So I trespassed.

150
07:49.659 --> 07:50.560
I'm sorry.

151
07:53.110 --> 07:54.909
I was probably zoning out.

152
08:13.090 --> 08:13.860
Little Jam.

153
08:14.290 --> 08:15.670
Are you sick?

154
08:17.370 --> 08:18.230
Oh...

155
08:18.710 --> 08:19.790
I'm feeling better now.

156
08:19.990 --> 08:21.290
I already took my medications.

157
08:25.830 --> 08:27.160
Have you eaten?

158
08:37.799 --> 08:39.370
Why are you like this?

159
08:41.950 --> 08:42.970
If that's the case...

160
08:43.970 --> 08:45.230
allow me to use the kitchen.

161
08:47.480 --> 08:48.170
Right.

162
08:50.860 --> 08:52.280
I didn't order anything.

163
08:52.470 --> 08:53.260
I did.

164
09:20.160 --> 09:20.860
Boiled crabs,

165
09:20.860 --> 09:22.060
your favorite.

166
09:22.270 --> 09:23.260
Where are the crabs?

167
09:23.600 --> 09:24.460
Here.

168
09:29.640 --> 09:30.650
I am not in the mood.

169
09:32.380 --> 09:33.100
Fine...

170
09:33.930 --> 09:35.290
Let me use the kitchen, then.

171
09:45.030 --> 09:46.060
Are you hungry?

172
09:46.920 --> 09:48.290
A little.

173
09:52.150 --> 09:53.470
Have a hot bowl of soup.

174
09:54.280 --> 09:55.310
It'll help you get better quicker.

175
09:58.510 --> 09:59.650
Thank you.

176
10:08.730 --> 10:10.470
Once it cools down, put it in the fridge.

177
10:10.690 --> 10:11.850
You can reheat it for tomorrow.

178
10:13.700 --> 10:14.900
Thank you.

179
10:17.590 --> 10:19.250
Can you change that word to something else?

180
10:20.170 --> 10:21.120
To what?

181
10:30.810 --> 10:32.160
Can I stay here for one night?

182
10:43.320 --> 10:44.190
Please?

183
10:46.750 --> 10:47.530
Please?

184
10:50.290 --> 10:51.200
Please?

185
10:53.390 --> 10:54.650
You rode your motorbike here?

186
10:54.650 --> 10:55.660
That's...right.

187
10:55.660 --> 10:57.210
I vroomed, vroomed, vroomed my way here

188
10:57.690 --> 10:59.130
so I could arrive sooner.

189
10:59.350 --> 11:01.060
I wanted to see you as soon as possible

190
11:01.080 --> 11:02.470
because I was worried about you.

191
11:03.460 --> 11:05.340
By the time he rides back from here...

192
11:05.370 --> 11:06.820
it'll already be late at night...

193
11:06.840 --> 11:09.520
He will probably fly down the road rather than just ride along.

194
11:09.840 --> 11:10.890
Dangerous...

195
11:11.520 --> 11:13.030
I am worried about him.

196
11:13.030 --> 11:13.780
Fine.

197
11:16.230 --> 11:17.120
Oh...

198
11:18.120 --> 11:20.860
The guest room has recently been repainted.

199
11:21.090 --> 11:22.520
It still smells like paint.

200
11:22.520 --> 11:23.120
Oh,

201
11:23.120 --> 11:24.230
that's nothing, Little Jam.

202
11:24.410 --> 11:25.760
I can sleep on the couch.

203
11:25.800 --> 11:26.470
I'm easygoing,

204
11:26.710 --> 11:27.590
not a picky eater.

205
11:27.790 --> 11:28.750
I'm also low-maintenance.

206
11:29.550 --> 11:30.790
I'll do just fine in any scenario.

207
11:31.400 --> 11:32.580
I can even sleep on the floor.

208
11:33.510 --> 11:34.050
Right.

209
11:34.820 --> 11:35.680
Sure.

210
11:39.390 --> 11:40.060
Yes!

211
11:40.060 --> 11:40.690
Hm?

212
11:42.990 --> 11:43.660
Ah.

213
11:44.330 --> 11:45.200
It's the black pepper.

214
11:45.370 --> 11:46.320
It stings.

215
11:46.780 --> 11:47.870
Are you okay?

216
11:47.870 --> 11:48.730
I am, yes.

217
11:49.110 --> 11:50.510
I really am.

218
11:56.190 --> 11:59.120
♫You're my love battery♫

219
11:59.120 --> 12:01.850
♫I've never been someone's priority♫

220
12:01.850 --> 12:04.320
♫Always been through heartbreak endlessly♫

221
12:05.260 --> 12:06.150
Yes!

222
12:09.030 --> 12:11.490
♫So many have come into my life and left me♫

223
12:11.490 --> 12:15.680
♫I've got nobody to stay right here beside me♫

224
12:16.510 --> 12:18.090
♫All alone...♫

225
12:24.250 --> 12:27.480
♫All alone, I'm restless night and day♫

226
12:27.480 --> 12:29.970
♫My heart just doesn't feel okay♫

227
12:29.970 --> 12:33.840
♫Like this, even paracetamol won't make it go away♫

228
12:33.840 --> 12:37.130
♫But then you came and stirred things up this way♫

229
12:37.130 --> 12:39.210
♫And my heart began to change♫

230
12:39.230 --> 12:42.460
♫I just want you to know…♫

231
12:42.460 --> 12:48.840
♫You're the positive energy in my life whenever I'm tired♫

232
12:48.840 --> 12:51.830
♫Just having you near...♫

233
12:51.830 --> 12:54.740
♫You charge my heart and bring me back to life♫

234
13:23.520 --> 13:24.640
Mr. Sarm.

235
13:32.290 --> 13:33.360
Yes, Little Jam?

236
13:34.180 --> 13:35.020
Here,

237
13:35.160 --> 13:36.340
your towel and clothes.

238
13:36.570 --> 13:38.500
Use the bathroom downstairs.

239
13:39.080 --> 13:40.720
As for the worn clothes,

240
13:41.010 --> 13:43.280
toss them in the rattan basket by the bathroom.

241
13:43.470 --> 13:45.170
I will dry the laundry.

242
13:46.830 --> 13:47.710
Okay.

243
13:49.370 --> 13:51.760
Let me get the bedding for you,

244
13:52.370 --> 13:53.650
but hang tight

245
13:54.110 --> 13:55.380
because I need to shower first.

246
13:55.660 --> 13:56.860
You can't, Little Jam.

247
14:00.300 --> 14:01.680
Just give yourself a sponge bath.

248
14:02.480 --> 14:03.870
You're still warm to the touch.

249
14:05.550 --> 14:07.070
I am taking a warm shower.

250
14:08.610 --> 14:09.710
Are you sure?

251
14:10.190 --> 14:10.590
Mm.

252
14:10.710 --> 14:11.490
Okay.

253
14:11.760 --> 14:12.460
Okay, sure.

254
14:13.140 --> 14:14.150
Okay.

255
15:14.270 --> 15:14.860
Little Jam.

256
15:16.650 --> 15:18.460
Here is your pillow and blanket, Mr. Sarm.

257
15:20.860 --> 15:21.490
Thank you.

258
15:30.760 --> 15:31.920
Sweet dreams.

259
15:33.290 --> 15:34.240
Sweet dreams.

260
15:39.280 --> 15:40.060
Little Jam.

261
15:47.720 --> 15:48.460
By the way...

262
15:49.230 --> 15:50.240
Is Juju not here?

263
15:50.720 --> 15:51.680
No,

264
15:52.060 --> 15:54.310
Mr. Sib borrowed her for a commercial shoot.

265
15:54.460 --> 15:55.470
Whoa...

266
15:56.390 --> 15:57.270
A celebrity cat.

267
15:57.380 --> 15:58.810
Did he pay you for this?

268
15:59.040 --> 15:59.990
He did not.

269
16:00.160 --> 16:01.010
He didn't?

270
16:01.190 --> 16:02.150
He did not hold back.

271
16:06.810 --> 16:07.660
With this...

272
16:07.900 --> 16:09.010
do you miss your cat?

273
16:09.390 --> 16:10.640
Of course, I do.

274
16:11.530 --> 16:13.470
It is not like we have never been apart before.

275
16:13.760 --> 16:16.100
I was away for months when I was in Pak Chong.

276
16:18.090 --> 16:18.950
Meow.

277
16:22.520 --> 16:24.050
I'll be your cat, then.

278
16:25.830 --> 16:27.590
My cat is only this tiny.

279
16:29.590 --> 16:30.680
Just like you.

280
16:32.480 --> 16:33.680
You're this tiny...

281
16:34.730 --> 16:35.770
But here...

282
16:37.950 --> 16:39.040
So chubby.

283
16:43.280 --> 16:45.160
I am going to bed now.

284
16:56.000 --> 16:56.860
Little Jam.

285
17:02.860 --> 17:04.920
Aren't we going to clear things up about what happened that day?

286
17:10.970 --> 17:12.460
Has it been seven days already?

287
17:14.089 --> 17:15.230
Why seven days?

288
17:18.460 --> 17:21.170
You said you would be mad at me for a week.

289
17:27.349 --> 17:28.490
I'm sorry...

290
17:30.330 --> 17:31.400
for turning away from you

291
17:32.160 --> 17:33.280
on that day.

292
17:48.840 --> 17:50.860
Well, you were upset.

293
17:54.330 --> 17:56.860
It was on me, too,

294
17:57.430 --> 17:58.800
for hiding the truth from you.

295
18:00.030 --> 18:02.060
I owe you an apology myself.

296
18:02.390 --> 18:03.240
No.

297
18:03.410 --> 18:04.510
No, Jam.

298
18:04.790 --> 18:05.840
It wasn't your fault.

299
18:06.150 --> 18:07.170
It was my fault

300
18:07.550 --> 18:08.480
for not listening to you.

301
18:09.290 --> 18:10.280
No,

302
18:10.840 --> 18:12.190
it was my fault.

303
18:12.750 --> 18:14.510
You asked me what I was doing,

304
18:15.030 --> 18:16.750
but I chose to double down.

305
18:16.750 --> 18:17.720
No, Little Jam.

306
18:19.430 --> 18:20.320
You're not to blame here.

307
18:21.210 --> 18:22.060
It's me.

308
18:22.870 --> 18:24.460
You were simply following Sib's order.

309
18:25.130 --> 18:25.870
I get it.

310
18:26.490 --> 18:27.290
It's on me.

311
18:28.060 --> 18:28.800
No...

312
18:35.610 --> 18:36.460
If that's the case,

313
18:37.320 --> 18:39.150
how about we share the blame between us?

314
18:44.120 --> 18:45.080
Mm, mm.

315
18:47.400 --> 18:48.460
Sure thing.

316
18:49.890 --> 18:51.160
By the way,

317
18:52.510 --> 18:54.190
are you not mad at me anymore?

318
18:56.900 --> 18:58.740
I never actually get mad at you.

319
18:59.450 --> 19:02.030
Forget being mad at you for seven days, seven months, or whatever.

320
19:02.750 --> 19:03.680
It is already killing me

321
19:03.850 --> 19:05.510
to be mad at you for seven hours.

322
19:10.650 --> 19:12.000
I thought...

323
19:13.630 --> 19:15.320
I would never get to see you again.

324
19:16.490 --> 19:17.570
Little Jam...

325
19:18.720 --> 19:20.070
what made you think that?

326
19:22.560 --> 19:24.840
You mean business when you get angry.

327
19:25.550 --> 19:27.480
You gave me a scary look, too.

328
19:33.200 --> 19:34.480
When we were on Ko Pha-ngan,

329
19:35.220 --> 19:36.190
I told you that

330
19:36.710 --> 19:38.090
I'd come see you when it was over,

331
19:38.720 --> 19:39.810
didn't I?

332
19:41.260 --> 19:42.460
On top of that...

333
19:43.040 --> 19:44.680
didn't I already tell you after the New Year's party...

334
19:48.350 --> 19:49.520
that I love you?

335
20:05.610 --> 20:06.670
"I love you, Little Jam."

336
20:06.750 --> 20:07.660
"I love you, Little Jam."

337
20:07.840 --> 20:08.860
"I love you, Little Jam."

338
20:09.260 --> 20:10.230
"I love you, Little Jam."

339
20:10.390 --> 20:11.260
"I love you, Little Jam."

340
20:11.850 --> 20:12.770
"I love you, Little Jam."

341
20:19.280 --> 20:19.950
Mr. Sarm?!

342
20:19.950 --> 20:21.170
Are you okay, Mr. Sarm?

343
20:21.640 --> 20:23.150
Was that you confessing your love without actually saying "love"?

344
20:25.910 --> 20:27.140
Mr. Sarm!

345
20:27.400 --> 20:28.400
Mr. Sarm, are you...

346
20:29.320 --> 20:30.790
It's okay if you can't say it right now.

347
20:30.970 --> 20:31.910
I'm right here,

348
20:32.550 --> 20:33.470
and I won't go anywhere.

349
20:33.730 --> 20:34.690
"I love you, Little Jam."

350
20:39.640 --> 20:40.460
Mr. Sarm!

351
20:41.040 --> 20:41.840
Mr. Sarm!

352
20:49.740 --> 20:51.700
Kindly adore this cat,

353
20:52.060 --> 20:52.690
too.

354
20:55.230 --> 20:56.820
If you like cats,

355
20:57.230 --> 20:58.060
then I'll be one.

356
21:10.640 --> 21:12.810
My cat has to get smooched.

357
21:13.660 --> 21:15.680
That is how I always smooch Juju.

358
21:27.600 --> 21:30.290
Get plenty of rest if you're sick, alright?

359
21:31.110 --> 21:31.660
Go to bed already.

360
21:31.660 --> 21:34.060
"I love you, Little Jam."

361
21:34.210 --> 21:35.260
Good night.

362
21:42.330 --> 21:44.020
Are you okay, Mr. Sarm?

363
21:44.480 --> 21:45.290
I am.

364
21:45.900 --> 21:47.260
I really am.

365
21:48.320 --> 21:49.290
I'm fine, really.

366
21:50.510 --> 21:52.250
I am hitting the hay, then.

367
21:52.590 --> 21:53.260
Bye-bye.

368
21:53.850 --> 21:54.810
Good night.

369
21:56.090 --> 21:56.830
Bye-bye...

370
22:03.530 --> 22:04.490
"I love you, Little Jam."

371
22:06.310 --> 22:08.830
♫Can I give a cutie like you a kiss? (Ohhhh, oh)♫

372
22:08.850 --> 22:10.560
♫Can I give you one more kiss? (Just you, only you, can it be you?)♫

373
22:10.580 --> 22:12.660
♫You♫

374
22:12.680 --> 22:14.190
♫Just a bit more (Hoo, woo)♫

375
22:14.190 --> 22:15.920
♫Can I kiss you one more time?♫

376
22:15.950 --> 22:17.680
♫Can I give you one more kiss?♫

377
22:17.680 --> 22:19.730
♫I'm not gonna lie (Hoo, woo)♫

378
22:19.750 --> 22:21.380
♫If I can't kiss you now, I'd lose my mind♫

379
22:21.400 --> 22:24.830
♫You, ou, ou, ou (If I can't kiss you now, I'd lose my mind)♫

380
22:24.850 --> 22:28.690
♫You, ou, ou, ou, ou (If I can't kiss you now, I'd lose my mind)♫

381
22:28.710 --> 22:30.120
[One day later]

382
22:30.140 --> 22:34.610
[Two days later]

383
23:04.670 --> 23:06.460
Mr. Sarm...

384
23:07.830 --> 23:08.470
What is it?

385
23:12.650 --> 23:14.010
I came to tell you that I'm leaving.

386
23:24.080 --> 23:25.350
Let me send you off downstairs.

387
23:25.660 --> 23:26.450
It's okay.

388
23:26.860 --> 23:28.060
Go back to bed.

389
23:28.670 --> 23:29.720
I came here to tell you that

390
23:29.970 --> 23:31.360
I made you xiaolongbao in the kitchen.

391
23:31.660 --> 23:32.860
Reheat it, and it's good to go.

392
23:33.520 --> 23:35.260
I've also made you fresh orange juice.

393
23:36.250 --> 23:37.660
Drink it while you're at the office

394
23:37.890 --> 23:38.860
so you'll feel refreshed.

395
23:40.190 --> 23:41.800
I sliced up a dragon fruit for you, too.

396
23:42.130 --> 23:43.210
It's in the fridge.

397
23:43.390 --> 23:44.510
The container is...

398
23:45.310 --> 23:46.060
light blue.

399
23:49.790 --> 23:51.510
You're so sweet.

400
23:56.280 --> 23:57.310
Then love me already.

401
24:11.480 --> 24:12.460
I'll be going now.

402
24:13.470 --> 24:14.860
Mm...

403
24:17.400 --> 24:18.950
Stay safe on the road.

404
24:19.350 --> 24:20.560
Do not go too fast,

405
24:20.710 --> 24:22.060
- understand? - Got it.

406
24:32.010 --> 24:32.860
I have to go now.

407
24:35.550 --> 24:36.250
Maybe not.

408
24:37.810 --> 24:38.570
- Just kidding. - I'll go now.

409
24:38.590 --> 24:39.770
You should get going now.

410
24:42.910 --> 24:43.660
I'm going now, alright?

411
24:44.410 --> 24:45.120
I'm leaving, okay?

412
24:45.430 --> 24:46.060
You heard that, right?

413
24:46.790 --> 24:47.510
I'm leaving now, okay?

414
24:47.950 --> 24:48.730
Alright.

415
24:49.280 --> 24:50.240
I'm going for real now, okay?

416
24:51.910 --> 24:52.640
I'll be going now.

417
24:53.530 --> 24:54.880
- I'm going now, okay? - Mm.

418
24:55.520 --> 24:56.720
Have a safe trip.

419
25:01.400 --> 25:02.080
I'm going now.

420
25:02.440 --> 25:03.110
Get going already.

421
25:03.880 --> 25:04.640
Bye-bye.

422
25:05.930 --> 25:06.460
Bye-bye.

423
25:06.840 --> 25:07.660
Bye-bye.

424
26:18.750 --> 26:19.890
This necklace...

425
26:21.400 --> 26:23.260
I once told Little Jam to never take it off.

426
26:24.460 --> 26:25.660
Yet he did.

427
26:31.200 --> 26:32.110
Soon...

428
26:34.060 --> 26:36.070
there's something I want to give him.

429
26:38.900 --> 26:41.300
I hope he'll forever keep it on.

430
27:08.160 --> 27:08.720
Right.

431
27:09.360 --> 27:10.530
Say the line.

432
27:10.920 --> 27:11.830
Right now?

433
27:12.800 --> 27:13.350
Mm.

434
27:13.870 --> 27:14.860
Right now.

435
27:15.370 --> 27:17.490
Are you waiting for a ribbon-cutting ceremony?

436
27:17.840 --> 27:19.010
Do you need me to call someone?

437
27:19.160 --> 27:20.070
Okay, okay.

438
27:22.710 --> 27:23.720
Here I go, okay?

439
27:23.870 --> 27:25.170
Yeah, please.

440
27:28.830 --> 27:29.520
Any minute now.

441
27:34.790 --> 27:35.260
Shall we begin?

442
27:35.260 --> 27:36.040
Come on!

443
27:36.460 --> 27:37.660
Don't rush me.

444
27:38.120 --> 27:39.430
Haven't you felt nervous before?

445
27:39.430 --> 27:41.030
Yes, I have,

446
27:41.520 --> 27:43.850
but it's been four hours already, Sarm.

447
27:43.850 --> 27:45.120
Are you going to marry him or what?

448
27:45.330 --> 27:46.060
Of course, I am.

449
27:46.530 --> 27:47.260
Just give me a second.

450
27:56.860 --> 27:58.360
No marriage, then, I suppose.

451
27:58.590 --> 27:59.240
Watch your mouth!

452
28:02.230 --> 28:03.760
How about this, Sarm?

453
28:04.210 --> 28:05.260
I think...

454
28:05.400 --> 28:06.250
you should try...

455
28:06.600 --> 28:08.480
relaxing

456
28:09.290 --> 28:10.060
and just say...

457
28:10.350 --> 28:12.270
what's on your mind.

458
28:13.800 --> 28:15.270
Where do I even start?

459
28:16.250 --> 28:17.640
I think...

460
28:17.950 --> 28:19.290
You can start with

461
28:19.510 --> 28:21.510
when you two first met.

462
28:23.110 --> 28:24.160
When I first met him,

463
28:24.810 --> 28:26.470
I pulled him by the shirt just like this.

464
28:27.430 --> 28:28.490
Then I thought

465
28:28.600 --> 28:31.000
that tiny guy was so chatty, annoying,

466
28:31.360 --> 28:32.390
and obnoxious.

467
28:32.860 --> 28:33.800
Is that it?

468
28:34.330 --> 28:35.040
Mm...

469
28:36.460 --> 28:37.660
I think...

470
28:37.890 --> 28:39.810
you need some rest, Sarm.

471
28:41.810 --> 28:42.710
Just...

472
28:43.310 --> 28:44.730
stay relaxed.

473
28:44.730 --> 28:46.060
I'll get you a drink.

474
28:46.610 --> 28:47.830
By the way...

475
28:47.830 --> 28:49.350
do you want gotu kola tea...

476
28:49.490 --> 28:50.860
or a drink of disappointment?

477
28:51.230 --> 28:52.060
Oh, damn you!

478
28:52.670 --> 28:53.110
Go there.

479
28:53.130 --> 28:54.220
Sit over there.

480
28:55.070 --> 28:55.480
Gosh.

481
28:55.480 --> 28:56.270
Sit down!

482
29:07.800 --> 29:08.390
Here.

483
29:11.080 --> 29:12.240
Orange juice again?!

484
29:12.240 --> 29:14.530
Why can't I ever escape oranges in this life?

485
29:14.530 --> 29:16.060
I want to go ask Dad,

486
29:16.350 --> 29:17.970
"Why the orange farm?!"

487
29:18.190 --> 29:19.820
Can we have a grapefruit farm instead?

488
29:19.840 --> 29:21.170
Gosh...

489
29:24.330 --> 29:25.490
But Little Jam loves oranges.

490
29:28.510 --> 29:30.120
Little Jam loves orange jam.

491
29:30.120 --> 29:30.760
Mm.

492
29:30.970 --> 29:32.040
Okay.

493
29:33.190 --> 29:34.760
The orange farm can stay, then.

494
29:36.640 --> 29:37.480
Thanks.

495
29:37.770 --> 29:38.470
Drink up.

496
29:42.070 --> 29:42.930
Refreshing!

497
29:42.930 --> 29:43.660
Mm.

498
29:44.130 --> 29:45.110
Good, good, good.

499
29:45.530 --> 29:46.290
Now, then...

500
29:46.290 --> 29:48.460
Now that you're refreshed, shall we...

501
29:49.210 --> 29:50.860
try again? Okay?

502
29:51.770 --> 29:53.010
Now, try...

503
29:53.680 --> 29:55.060
talking about

504
29:55.660 --> 29:57.230
your first impression.

505
29:58.200 --> 29:59.070
Think about it.

506
30:01.360 --> 30:02.120
Do you have any?

507
30:03.320 --> 30:03.790
Yeah.

508
30:04.200 --> 30:05.260
Tell me about it.

509
30:12.170 --> 30:12.830
Mm.

510
30:19.930 --> 30:20.480
Gosh.

511
30:21.310 --> 30:22.060
Listen.

512
30:22.330 --> 30:23.260
I'm

513
30:23.440 --> 30:25.200
very impressed by him.

514
30:25.330 --> 30:26.250
He's talented,

515
30:26.370 --> 30:27.130
smart,

516
30:27.290 --> 30:28.060
a fast learner,

517
30:28.360 --> 30:29.050
a runner,

518
30:29.260 --> 30:30.190
- Right... - a hearty eater,

519
30:30.690 --> 30:31.430
and a debater.

520
30:32.030 --> 30:32.650
Oh,

521
30:32.670 --> 30:33.520
he also crashes out a lot.

522
30:33.950 --> 30:34.760
He's just so damn cute.

523
30:35.800 --> 30:36.870
He's my jam.

524
30:38.000 --> 30:40.060
Gosh, Sarm...

525
30:40.960 --> 30:42.460
If I were Jam,

526
30:42.570 --> 30:43.970
I would've rejected you.

527
30:45.120 --> 30:46.290
You're as stiff as a rock.

528
30:46.520 --> 30:47.390
Try again.

529
30:49.360 --> 30:50.040
You've got this.

530
31:06.160 --> 31:08.450
♫I want to be called your lover♫

531
31:09.920 --> 31:11.260
♫I want your arm entwined with mine♫

532
31:11.880 --> 31:13.070
♫Like what lovers do♫

533
31:15.200 --> 31:16.040
That... That was decent.

534
31:16.060 --> 31:17.260
Try to keep it going.

535
31:19.210 --> 31:20.350
Here's the deal.

536
31:21.810 --> 31:23.260
We might have started

537
31:23.260 --> 31:24.880
on the wrong foot,

538
31:25.660 --> 31:26.860
but

539
31:27.030 --> 31:28.790
my feelings have changed.

540
31:30.670 --> 31:31.660
Right now,

541
31:33.280 --> 31:34.450
I can't live without you.

542
31:35.470 --> 31:36.190
Yeah.

543
31:37.430 --> 31:38.860
If I don't get to see you,

544
31:39.710 --> 31:41.260
I'll probably miss you to death.

545
31:41.990 --> 31:43.310
Everyone knows,

546
31:43.810 --> 31:44.860
as do the ghosts

547
31:44.860 --> 31:46.250
and the spirits at the orange farm,

548
31:46.800 --> 31:47.630
that...

549
31:47.990 --> 31:49.280
I'm a few cards short of a full deck.

550
31:50.730 --> 31:51.310
Mm.

551
31:51.310 --> 31:52.060
It's dead obvious.

552
31:53.240 --> 31:54.440
But you...

553
31:56.100 --> 31:57.300
make me

554
31:57.840 --> 31:59.260
complete.

555
31:59.680 --> 32:00.970
Wow...

556
32:01.240 --> 32:02.400
Now, my life

557
32:02.640 --> 32:04.060
can't go on without you.

558
32:09.190 --> 32:10.490
Why is that, you may ask?

559
32:14.970 --> 32:16.790
Because you're everything to me.

560
32:17.770 --> 32:18.460
I...

561
32:19.400 --> 32:20.530
I love you.

562
32:21.000 --> 32:22.200
I love you very much

563
32:22.330 --> 32:23.990
with all the heart one person

564
32:25.910 --> 32:27.070
can possibly give.

565
32:37.950 --> 32:39.450
From now on,

566
32:39.730 --> 32:41.260
I want you to be the first person I wake up to

567
32:42.600 --> 32:44.860
and the last before going to bed.

568
32:45.150 --> 32:46.960
I want to see you every day

569
32:47.970 --> 32:50.030
because you're the very breath I breathe.

570
32:52.800 --> 32:54.080
After all of that,

571
32:55.660 --> 32:57.310
you can probably guess

572
32:57.310 --> 32:58.720
what I'll say next, can't you?

573
33:03.570 --> 33:04.480
That's right.

574
33:05.090 --> 33:06.810
The next thing I want to say is that...

575
33:07.930 --> 33:09.480
the secret to making tasty boiled crabs

576
33:09.770 --> 33:11.150
is to add Himalayan salt.

577
33:13.360 --> 33:14.860
You've got it, Sarm.

578
33:15.030 --> 33:15.480
Mm.

579
33:15.710 --> 33:16.360
Perfect!

580
33:16.360 --> 33:17.260
I think it'll work.

581
33:17.260 --> 33:17.970
Trust me.

582
33:17.970 --> 33:18.880
It's good.

583
33:19.240 --> 33:20.120
Isn't it?

584
33:20.120 --> 33:20.860
Mm.

585
33:21.270 --> 33:22.060
Gosh...

586
33:22.560 --> 33:23.890
I'm a goddamn genius.

587
33:25.120 --> 33:27.350
But I think you can do more.

588
33:27.550 --> 33:29.950
With the quote "I love you very much,"

589
33:30.250 --> 33:31.660
make it sound

590
33:31.660 --> 33:34.140
much longer.

591
33:35.260 --> 33:36.800
It'll make it even better.

592
33:36.940 --> 33:37.630
Really?

593
33:37.970 --> 33:38.470
Of course.

594
33:38.470 --> 33:39.920
Won't it sound over the top?

595
33:40.060 --> 33:40.960
I don't think so.

596
33:40.960 --> 33:42.380
It'll sound more natural,

597
33:42.800 --> 33:44.180
for someone like you, that is.

598
33:47.430 --> 33:48.460
Are you taking a shot at me?

599
33:48.880 --> 33:50.180
No, you're imagining it.

600
33:55.250 --> 33:56.000
Gosh.

601
33:57.230 --> 34:00.200
♫You're my love battery♫

602
34:00.220 --> 34:02.840
♫I've never been someone's priority♫

603
34:02.860 --> 34:05.570
♫Always been through heartbreak endlessly♫

604
34:05.590 --> 34:07.190
"I love you, Little Jam."

605
34:09.110 --> 34:10.060
Smooch.

606
34:14.570 --> 34:15.690
This heart is yours.

607
34:17.489 --> 34:22.300
♫Filling this heart that once felt empty inside♫

608
34:22.320 --> 34:27.690
♫The positive vibe in my life whenever I'm tired♫

609
34:27.710 --> 34:30.960
♫Just having you near…♫

610
34:49.650 --> 34:51.710
Where are you taking me to?

611
34:52.480 --> 34:53.920
Today,

612
34:56.860 --> 34:59.000
I'll take you scuba diving to see the beautiful coral

613
34:59.020 --> 35:01.180
and sea anemones.

614
35:01.410 --> 35:04.450
Then, we'll have a wonderful lunch.

615
35:04.480 --> 35:06.880
Mind you, the restaurant has amazing reviews.

616
35:07.000 --> 35:08.420
Then, we'll take a nap...

617
35:08.440 --> 35:10.450
recharging ourselves a bit.

618
35:10.470 --> 35:11.530
Uh...

619
35:11.580 --> 35:14.110
Once the sun goes down a bit, we'll hike in the woods

620
35:14.140 --> 35:15.840
and watch a breathtaking sunset!

621
35:17.290 --> 35:18.360
But right now,

622
35:18.520 --> 35:19.850
let's get something to eat.

623
35:20.000 --> 35:21.780
An army marches on its stomach.

624
35:25.840 --> 35:27.110
And...

625
35:28.090 --> 35:30.310
What about the banana boat and parasailing?

626
35:31.000 --> 35:32.070
I want to try them both.

627
35:33.510 --> 35:34.780
How about tomorrow?

628
35:35.530 --> 35:36.660
Not today?

629
35:36.880 --> 35:38.890
How about changing the afternoon nap

630
35:39.100 --> 35:41.050
to parasailing instead?

631
35:45.030 --> 35:46.360
Not a great idea, Jam.

632
35:46.390 --> 35:47.290
It goes against my plan.

633
35:47.460 --> 35:48.640
What plan?

634
35:49.210 --> 35:49.860
Well...

635
35:51.110 --> 35:52.990
Well, the hiking.

636
35:54.380 --> 35:55.190
Hm...

637
35:55.220 --> 35:56.000
Uh...

638
35:56.020 --> 35:56.690
But

639
35:56.710 --> 35:59.690
I'll take you for extreme activities all over the island tomorrow.

640
35:59.710 --> 36:01.690
You can do everything you want.

641
36:01.800 --> 36:02.890
Okay?

642
36:05.660 --> 36:06.820
Are you sure?

643
36:07.110 --> 36:07.860
Mm.

644
36:08.920 --> 36:09.690
Mm,

645
36:09.900 --> 36:10.800
alright, then.

646
36:11.490 --> 36:12.950
That's so sweet of you.

647
36:17.440 --> 36:18.490
Let's have a meal, then.

648
36:33.670 --> 36:35.290
I don't want to have a meal now.

649
36:36.250 --> 36:37.660
I want to have you.

650
36:39.580 --> 36:41.290
It's like what they say,

651
36:42.600 --> 36:44.290
jam goes well with anything.

652
36:46.020 --> 36:47.220
Hey!

653
36:47.870 --> 36:49.310
We are having a meal, right?

654
36:56.180 --> 36:56.890
Let's go.

655
37:00.490 --> 37:02.580
Where are you taking me to?

656
37:02.960 --> 37:03.910
Hey! Stop.

657
37:03.930 --> 37:05.270
Stop...

658
37:05.580 --> 37:06.490
Stop it!

659
37:12.490 --> 37:13.690
Here, Little Jam.

660
37:13.950 --> 37:14.670
Thank you.

661
37:14.670 --> 37:15.200
Come here.

662
37:16.090 --> 37:16.960
Here.

663
37:21.720 --> 37:22.600
Slowly, okay?

664
37:22.600 --> 37:23.500
- Be careful. - Right.

665
37:26.430 --> 37:27.270
Right here.

666
37:39.560 --> 37:40.470
Here we are.

667
37:40.470 --> 37:41.670
- Right... - Yay.

668
37:43.620 --> 37:44.560
Be careful, alright?

669
37:44.780 --> 37:46.520
If something happens to you,

670
37:46.660 --> 37:47.540
my heart will break.

671
37:50.890 --> 37:52.090
See that over there?

672
37:52.090 --> 37:52.860
Isn't it beautiful?

673
37:53.480 --> 37:54.470
That island over there?

674
37:54.490 --> 37:55.690
Yes.

675
37:57.300 --> 37:58.090
Hey...

676
37:58.210 --> 37:59.140
Mr. Sarm.

677
37:59.140 --> 37:59.560
Hm?

678
37:59.560 --> 38:01.070
I looked so goofy.

679
38:01.130 --> 38:02.550
How so, Little Jam?

680
38:02.810 --> 38:03.400
Take a look.

681
38:03.420 --> 38:04.450
- In every way. - See?

682
38:04.950 --> 38:06.290
You look really adorable, Little Jam.

683
38:06.320 --> 38:07.150
I'll

684
38:07.360 --> 38:09.280
make a print that covers the whole wall,

685
38:09.280 --> 38:11.120
and I'll display it behind the bed

686
38:11.220 --> 38:12.990
so I get to see your face every day.

687
38:13.520 --> 38:14.300
I'm serious.

688
38:14.780 --> 38:16.090
Thinking about it already makes me happy.

689
38:19.110 --> 38:20.140
Ridiculous.

690
38:23.900 --> 38:24.450
Here.

691
38:24.620 --> 38:25.940
Let me take photos of you instead.

692
38:25.940 --> 38:26.710
Oh, okay.

693
38:29.010 --> 38:29.380
Alright, alright.

694
38:29.400 --> 38:30.190
Let me pose real quick.

695
38:30.220 --> 38:30.820
Alright.

696
38:32.140 --> 38:33.370
Make sure you look handsome, okay?

697
38:33.390 --> 38:34.060
I already am.

698
38:35.600 --> 38:36.300
Three,

699
38:36.320 --> 38:36.890
two,

700
38:36.890 --> 38:37.480
one.

701
38:41.450 --> 38:42.170
How is it?

702
38:42.190 --> 38:44.840
Am I handsome enough to be the man of your heart?

703
38:46.010 --> 38:47.210
Mm...

704
38:48.510 --> 38:49.940
I think the likes of you

705
38:50.120 --> 38:51.790
work better as the bad guy against my heart.

706
38:51.790 --> 38:53.070
Oh, Little Jam.

707
38:53.260 --> 38:54.710
If I were a bad guy,

708
38:54.710 --> 38:56.190
I'd be the one...

709
38:56.470 --> 38:57.890
who loves you deeply,

710
38:58.490 --> 39:00.890
from the very bottom of my heart.

711
39:02.290 --> 39:03.430
The very bottom of your heart?

712
39:03.430 --> 39:04.310
Yes.

713
39:04.480 --> 39:05.950
Now, now, let's take more selfies.

714
39:08.480 --> 39:09.050
Three,

715
39:09.050 --> 39:09.390
two,

716
39:09.390 --> 39:09.880
one.

717
39:12.250 --> 39:12.730
Hm.

718
39:14.170 --> 39:16.650
My cheek will get bruised at this point.

719
39:18.590 --> 39:18.870
Ha, ha.

720
39:18.870 --> 39:20.080
It won't get bruised that easily.

721
39:23.010 --> 39:24.020
Mm...

722
39:24.800 --> 39:26.120
Oh...

723
39:27.520 --> 39:28.570
Shooting from every angle.

724
39:30.010 --> 39:31.660
Are you a vacuum cleaner or what?

725
39:31.660 --> 39:32.270
Yes...

726
39:32.270 --> 39:33.310
Oh, Little Jam!

727
39:33.570 --> 39:34.180
Dolphins!

728
39:34.360 --> 39:35.260
- Whoa! - Mm.

729
39:44.230 --> 39:45.880
Shooting in 360 degrees.

730
39:46.060 --> 39:47.260
We'll get shots from every angle.

731
39:48.130 --> 39:48.690
Ha, ha.

732
39:48.690 --> 39:50.320
You teased me again.

733
40:02.480 --> 40:02.860
What?!

734
40:02.880 --> 40:03.670
Little Jam,

735
40:03.800 --> 40:05.050
what's that box?

736
40:05.260 --> 40:05.680
A box?

737
40:05.680 --> 40:06.990
Over there. Right there.

738
40:07.450 --> 40:08.730
Maybe there's something in it.

739
40:08.970 --> 40:10.310
Maybe it's a treasure.

740
40:10.530 --> 40:11.620
Go pick it up.

741
40:11.790 --> 40:12.890
Come on, Little Jam.

742
40:12.960 --> 40:14.100
I would rather not.

743
40:16.020 --> 40:16.640
It's okay.

744
40:16.640 --> 40:17.510
If that's the case, I'll...

745
40:17.650 --> 40:18.460
I'll... I'll...

746
40:19.110 --> 40:20.560
Let us not, Mr. Sarm.

747
40:20.560 --> 40:22.060
In movies, they say...

748
40:22.290 --> 40:24.460
we should not touch someone else's stuff without permission.

749
40:25.090 --> 40:26.200
Come on, it's okay.

750
40:26.200 --> 40:28.880
You would be in trouble if the owner came back and looked for it.

751
40:28.880 --> 40:29.480
Maybe it's not...

752
40:29.480 --> 40:31.660
There are no shamans here either.

753
40:32.830 --> 40:34.870
Little Jam, there's nobody here, though.

754
40:34.870 --> 40:35.390
Take a peek inside the box...

755
40:35.390 --> 40:36.310
Exactly.

756
40:36.310 --> 40:37.360
There is nobody here.

757
40:37.360 --> 40:38.860
And your feng shui master

758
40:38.860 --> 40:40.430
is back in Pak Chong.

759
40:40.640 --> 40:42.010
He cannot save you in time.

760
40:42.710 --> 40:43.920
Just open it for a second.

761
40:44.150 --> 40:44.480
It's okay, we'll...

762
40:44.480 --> 40:44.990
No!

763
40:46.190 --> 40:46.920
Let us not.

764
40:47.450 --> 40:48.240
But...

765
40:48.870 --> 40:49.470
Just a quick peek.

766
40:49.470 --> 40:50.670
No, stop it, Mr. Sarm!

767
40:50.670 --> 40:51.210
Try...

768
40:51.210 --> 40:51.930
If you open it,

769
40:51.930 --> 40:53.510
we will break up.

770
40:55.490 --> 40:56.590
But, Little Jam...

771
40:57.190 --> 40:58.480
Not even a quick peek?

772
41:01.550 --> 41:03.120
But...

773
41:04.270 --> 41:04.830
Oh...

774
41:04.830 --> 41:05.800
You're right, Little Jam.

775
41:05.800 --> 41:07.190
Who knows what's inside that box.

776
41:07.190 --> 41:08.860
If there's something dangerous inside,

777
41:09.080 --> 41:10.170
- nobody can save us, right? - Yes.

778
41:10.170 --> 41:11.010
Let's leave it there.

779
41:11.260 --> 41:12.650
Also, it is getting dark.

780
41:12.650 --> 41:13.090
Mm.

781
41:13.090 --> 41:14.240
Let us head back, shall we?

782
41:14.240 --> 41:15.030
Yeah, there are swarms of mosquitoes, too.

783
41:15.030 --> 41:15.800
Let's get going, then.

784
41:15.800 --> 41:16.440
- Let us. - Mm.

785
41:17.950 --> 41:18.880
Little Jam...

786
41:26.510 --> 41:28.060
I got you a surprise.

787
41:29.070 --> 41:29.760
Gosh...

788
41:29.760 --> 41:32.320
I even styled my hair to look this cool.

789
41:33.190 --> 41:34.060
There goes my plan.

790
41:34.530 --> 41:35.510
Little Jam.

791
41:35.750 --> 41:36.640
Mr. Sarm!

792
41:36.640 --> 41:37.800
Hurry up, Mr. Sarm!

793
41:37.800 --> 41:38.860
Okay, Little Jam.

794
41:39.110 --> 41:40.060
Wait for me.

795
41:40.060 --> 41:40.850
I'm on my way.

796
41:42.460 --> 41:43.120
Hey.

797
41:43.550 --> 41:44.730
Get out of there already, Mr. Sarm...

798
41:51.490 --> 41:52.570
Mr. Sarm!

799
41:53.420 --> 41:54.000
Yes?

800
41:54.310 --> 41:55.280
Let us get going.

801
41:58.140 --> 41:59.630
Quickly, Mr. Sarm!

802
41:59.630 --> 42:00.670
It is getting dark.

803
42:00.670 --> 42:01.430
Okay, okay.

804
42:01.430 --> 42:02.080
I'm coming.

805
42:02.210 --> 42:03.010
Little Jam...

806
42:17.260 --> 42:23.260
[Uncle Mai's Kitchen]

807
42:23.400 --> 42:24.210
Little Jam,

808
42:24.230 --> 42:24.790
look.

809
42:24.810 --> 42:26.110
I have dinner prepared for us.

810
42:26.130 --> 42:27.110
It looks so delicious.

811
42:27.320 --> 42:28.040
Are you hungry?

812
42:28.060 --> 42:29.060
You are, aren't you?

813
42:29.080 --> 42:30.440
Let's have dinner, then.

814
42:30.460 --> 42:31.110
Come on.

815
42:31.660 --> 42:33.470
Wow...

816
42:33.470 --> 42:34.830
Ta-da, ta-da...

817
42:34.830 --> 42:36.310
Dun-dun, ta-da, ta-da

818
42:36.310 --> 42:36.790
Da-da

819
42:36.790 --> 42:38.860
I have to leave early tomorrow.

820
42:43.070 --> 42:45.250
I cannot stay any longer.

821
42:46.790 --> 42:50.050
Mr. Sib's client flew here from Hong Kong with his family,

822
42:50.390 --> 42:52.060
and he wants me to host them.

823
43:05.510 --> 43:06.460
But...

824
43:10.870 --> 43:12.750
Isn't tomorrow your day off, Little Jam?

825
43:13.660 --> 43:15.240
We also have plans.

826
43:17.130 --> 43:18.130
Oh, right.

827
43:18.130 --> 43:20.280
Sib has many secretaries.

828
43:21.150 --> 43:22.750
Can't he let one of them handle the job?

829
43:26.990 --> 43:30.810
I already hosted the client's family,

830
43:32.160 --> 43:34.640
so I knew

831
43:35.260 --> 43:36.890
what he liked

832
43:37.440 --> 43:40.600
and what his wife and kids were allergic to.

833
43:50.430 --> 43:51.270
And...

834
43:53.470 --> 43:54.810
Can't you stay, Little Jam?

835
44:19.390 --> 44:21.090
Do you see these raindrops?

836
44:23.710 --> 44:24.460
They...

837
44:25.310 --> 44:26.670
They're my teardrops.

838
44:37.090 --> 44:38.310
Mr. Sarm...

839
44:39.480 --> 44:41.260
I cannot say no to Mr. Sib.

840
45:19.210 --> 45:20.530
Can I come with you, then?

841
45:23.770 --> 45:24.460
Please?

842
45:24.790 --> 45:25.660
Can I come with you?

843
45:35.940 --> 45:37.630
That is not possible.

844
45:43.250 --> 45:44.630
Can you not leave, Little Jam?

845
45:47.260 --> 45:49.310
It's really hard to find time

846
45:49.310 --> 45:50.490
for a trip together.

847
45:55.770 --> 45:58.450
You can stay here and enjoy the vacation.

848
46:00.870 --> 46:02.050
Without you here,

849
46:03.340 --> 46:05.230
this place means nothing.

850
46:06.150 --> 46:07.160
I'm not staying.

851
46:12.720 --> 46:14.270
It's tomorrow no matter what, right?

852
46:19.970 --> 46:20.860
Mm.

853
46:22.790 --> 46:23.410
Oh, oh.

854
46:23.410 --> 46:24.460
Mr. Sarm...

855
46:27.400 --> 46:29.070
If my life were a soap opera,

856
46:29.490 --> 46:30.990
it'd be called

857
46:31.490 --> 46:33.110
"Traiphop's Tears."

858
46:33.710 --> 46:35.040
The antagonist

859
46:35.150 --> 46:36.460
would be none other

860
46:36.630 --> 46:38.310
than my own older brother.

861
46:39.110 --> 46:41.830
He assigned the task at such perfect timing.

862
47:05.050 --> 47:06.760
You returned earlier than expected.

863
47:10.190 --> 47:11.850
Can you prepare gotu kola tea for me?

864
47:12.080 --> 47:13.480
Make me a full pot.

865
47:14.710 --> 47:15.770
I'll come back here to enjoy it.

866
47:16.720 --> 47:17.440
No problem.

867
47:36.080 --> 47:37.510
Right. Jab and use your hips.

868
47:37.510 --> 47:38.310
Try jabbing.

869
47:39.120 --> 47:39.850
Good.

870
47:40.850 --> 47:41.730
That's good.

871
47:43.290 --> 47:43.870
Not like that.

872
47:44.040 --> 47:44.570
Oh?

873
47:45.280 --> 47:46.060
Mr. Sarm,

874
47:46.360 --> 47:49.060
did you change your mind and come back to welcome our new boxers?

875
47:50.790 --> 47:51.810
Not exactly.

876
47:52.490 --> 47:53.790
How many boxers are in this batch?

877
47:53.790 --> 47:55.280
Two, actually.

878
47:55.550 --> 47:56.710
But don't worry,

879
47:56.800 --> 47:59.240
we've got both an amateur and a professional.

880
47:59.260 --> 48:00.200
They're all talented.

881
48:00.200 --> 48:01.510
They're not hard to train.

882
48:02.320 --> 48:03.600
By the way, Mr. Sarm,

883
48:03.600 --> 48:05.080
aren't you going to give them a welcome match?

884
48:05.490 --> 48:07.160
Let them shine on their own.

885
48:07.550 --> 48:09.110
You've got a great body,

886
48:09.110 --> 48:11.130
and everyone in Pak Chong knows that

887
48:11.130 --> 48:12.770
you're the real deal.

888
48:15.650 --> 48:16.410
Fine.

889
48:16.500 --> 48:17.230
I'll hop in.

890
48:17.720 --> 48:18.300
See you soon.

891
49:10.980 --> 49:13.980
[My Little Jam]

892
49:32.090 --> 49:33.690
A smartphone can be charged,

893
49:34.590 --> 49:35.530
but look at me.

894
49:38.070 --> 49:39.310
Nobody's charging my heart.

895
49:58.690 --> 49:59.840
Gosh...

896
50:09.620 --> 50:10.850
[I arrived safe and sound

897
50:10.880 --> 50:12.340
Do not worry; I will be busy working

898
50:12.370 --> 50:13.470
Might not get to answer your calls]

899
50:16.490 --> 50:22.600
[My Little Jam]

900
50:25.070 --> 50:26.200
[Sarm: Hey]

901
50:26.230 --> 50:27.550
[Sarm: Still occupied? What are you doing? Have you eaten yet?]

902
50:27.570 --> 50:28.500
[Sarm: I'm home, actually; I left soon after you did

903
50:28.530 --> 50:29.190
Being there alone felt too empty]

904
50:29.210 --> 50:30.180
[Sarm: I had fun boxing today; I got destroyed by a pro

905
50:30.210 --> 50:31.290
It all hurts, but it's not as bad as not seeing you, Little Jam]

906
50:31.320 --> 50:32.510
[Sarm: Take care of yourself over there, eat lots of good food,

907
50:32.530 --> 50:33.400
get plenty of rest, and don't overwork; I'm worried about you]

908
50:33.880 --> 50:34.570
Whoa!

909
50:35.760 --> 50:36.690
You're looking at me?

910
50:37.210 --> 50:39.050
You look at me every day, huh?

911
50:40.310 --> 50:41.260
Look at the wall instead.

912
50:58.640 --> 51:00.460
You seem troubled,

913
51:00.910 --> 51:02.480
as if you've had a fight with your partner.

914
51:04.870 --> 51:05.840
Mr. Sib...

915
51:07.360 --> 51:08.860
You are not the real Mr. Sib.

916
51:09.040 --> 51:11.010
Give me back my real boss.

917
51:12.260 --> 51:13.430
I'll ask you again.

918
51:14.010 --> 51:15.480
What's troubling your mind?

919
51:17.130 --> 51:19.910
If Mr. Sarm disappeared again,

920
51:20.410 --> 51:22.060
what would you do?

921
51:23.470 --> 51:24.720
It's simple, really.

922
51:25.330 --> 51:26.960
I'll send you to find him again,

923
51:27.240 --> 51:28.370
but this time,

924
51:28.370 --> 51:29.730
if you can't find him,

925
51:29.870 --> 51:31.060
do not come back.

926
51:31.430 --> 51:33.510
Even if you have to turn the whole world upside down,

927
51:33.890 --> 51:35.260
you have to find him.

928
51:35.600 --> 51:37.630
I have probably used up all my luck.

929
51:38.710 --> 51:39.310
Oh?

930
51:39.510 --> 51:40.400
Why is that?

931
51:41.750 --> 51:43.130
What did you do to my brother again?

932
51:43.480 --> 51:44.530
Sarm...

933
51:44.910 --> 51:46.700
He's my precious little brother.

934
51:48.550 --> 51:50.130
I have not done anything,

935
51:51.480 --> 51:52.640
but I do not understand

936
51:52.640 --> 51:55.000
why he looked that upset either.

937
51:57.110 --> 51:58.400
I just talked to my dad,

938
51:59.010 --> 52:01.120
and he said Sarm had just gotten back from Ko Pha-ngan

939
52:01.360 --> 52:03.030
and looked sad.

940
52:03.280 --> 52:04.440
He has returned?

941
52:04.760 --> 52:05.520
Mm.

942
52:06.130 --> 52:07.180
Oh...

943
52:07.200 --> 52:09.100
You went there with him, right?

944
52:10.670 --> 52:11.690
I'm so sorry

945
52:11.710 --> 52:12.760
for asking you to come here.

946
52:13.290 --> 52:15.140
I interrupted your time together on your trip, right?

947
52:15.360 --> 52:16.290
No, not at all.

948
52:16.480 --> 52:16.870
Uh,

949
52:16.870 --> 52:18.460
I was just on vacation.

950
52:20.310 --> 52:21.160
Here's the deal.

951
52:21.790 --> 52:23.260
How about I teach you

952
52:23.560 --> 52:25.890
how to stop saying one thing and meaning another?

953
52:28.310 --> 52:29.770
How much is this training?

954
52:30.280 --> 52:32.480
If it is affordable, then I will sign up.

955
52:33.090 --> 52:34.600
You're good at dodging the subject.

956
52:35.590 --> 52:36.280
At any rate,

957
52:37.380 --> 52:39.720
if something is troubling you,

958
52:40.390 --> 52:41.850
don't hold it for too long.

959
52:42.210 --> 52:43.930
Don't complicate things.

960
52:44.600 --> 52:46.050
I know you're talented,

961
52:46.690 --> 52:47.590
and you already know

962
52:47.830 --> 52:49.250
what you should do.

963
52:50.290 --> 52:52.470
If I delayed things any longer,

964
52:52.710 --> 52:54.460
Mr. Sarm might lose himself.

965
52:54.870 --> 52:56.310
He might not just take a trip to an island

966
52:56.530 --> 52:58.690
but to outer space.

967
52:58.870 --> 52:59.810
Mr. Sib.

968
53:01.030 --> 53:03.310
May I go and follow my heart?

969
53:04.330 --> 53:05.260
Go ahead.

970
53:05.760 --> 53:07.520
I always support you.

971
53:07.920 --> 53:08.860
Also...

972
53:09.120 --> 53:10.280
follow it through.

973
53:10.770 --> 53:11.930
Once you reach your destination,

974
53:12.050 --> 53:13.310
do come back and tell me about it.

975
53:13.660 --> 53:14.860
Thank you, Mr. Sib!

976
53:14.970 --> 53:17.260
May your success shine

977
53:17.260 --> 53:19.040
brighter than fireworks.

978
53:19.170 --> 53:20.170
Get going already

979
53:20.170 --> 53:21.190
before it's too late.

980
53:21.360 --> 53:22.450
Right, Mr. Sib.

981
53:23.430 --> 53:24.460
I will be on my way, then.

982
53:33.200 --> 53:34.060
Song.

983
53:34.270 --> 53:35.050
Jam.

984
53:35.050 --> 53:35.710
Take a seat.

985
53:35.710 --> 53:36.460
Thank you.

986
53:39.270 --> 53:40.370
What brings you here?

987
53:40.370 --> 53:42.080
Why are you in such a rush?

988
53:42.320 --> 53:43.660
I need help.

989
53:44.320 --> 53:45.840
Sarm is mad at me,

990
53:45.840 --> 53:47.570
and I am here to make it up to him.

991
53:47.930 --> 53:49.950
Sarm is mad at you, really?

992
53:50.520 --> 53:51.010
And...

993
53:51.320 --> 53:52.730
How was the trip to Ko Pha-ngan?

994
53:52.920 --> 53:53.870
Can you tell me about it?

995
53:54.110 --> 53:56.670
An urgent task came up, so I had to leave early.

996
53:56.770 --> 53:58.550
Mr. Sarm seemed a little upset, too.

997
53:58.550 --> 54:00.090
He did not pick up the phone

998
54:00.170 --> 54:01.660
or reply to my texts.

999
54:02.430 --> 54:03.800
And... did...

1000
54:04.530 --> 54:05.550
Did Sarm...

1001
54:05.570 --> 54:07.660
Did he give you the ring?

1002
54:08.860 --> 54:09.750
The ring?

1003
54:10.590 --> 54:11.550
The ring.

1004
54:12.320 --> 54:13.530
What ring?

1005
54:14.690 --> 54:15.620
Well...

1006
54:16.000 --> 54:17.080
When...

1007
54:17.170 --> 54:18.250
someone...

1008
54:18.250 --> 54:19.530
gives another person a ring,

1009
54:19.800 --> 54:21.840
what...does that mean?

1010
54:22.320 --> 54:23.520
They want them to sell it?

1011
54:25.640 --> 54:26.690
No, no.

1012
54:26.690 --> 54:27.550
Jam...

1013
54:28.060 --> 54:29.390
Picture this.

1014
54:29.630 --> 54:30.670
If

1015
54:30.670 --> 54:32.860
someone

1016
54:32.860 --> 54:34.530
wants to give you a ring,

1017
54:35.040 --> 54:37.910
what's their intention?

1018
54:40.570 --> 54:43.450
Tick-tock, tick-tock, tick-tock.

1019
54:43.870 --> 54:45.340
To marry me?

1020
54:45.420 --> 54:46.900
Excellent, Jam!

1021
54:47.590 --> 54:48.690
The intention is to marry.

1022
54:48.970 --> 54:50.480
Now, then,

1023
54:50.720 --> 54:51.840
Sarm

1024
54:52.060 --> 54:53.770
wants to give you

1025
54:53.770 --> 54:54.840
his ring...

1026
54:56.010 --> 54:58.730
This means that he wants to...

1027
54:59.130 --> 55:01.000
He wants to marry me?

1028
55:01.000 --> 55:01.770
Well done!

1029
55:01.770 --> 55:03.810
You hit the nail on the head, Jam.

1030
55:04.060 --> 55:05.260
But that is not possible.

1031
55:05.410 --> 55:07.130
It is possible, Jam.

1032
55:07.920 --> 55:09.480
Think about it.

1033
55:09.830 --> 55:11.080
Did

1034
55:11.080 --> 55:13.440
Sarm ask you...

1035
55:13.660 --> 55:15.050
to look at a certain box?

1036
55:16.590 --> 55:17.910
What's that box?

1037
55:18.040 --> 55:18.460
A box?

1038
55:18.460 --> 55:19.660
Over there. Right there.

1039
55:21.130 --> 55:22.310
That box...

1040
55:23.870 --> 55:25.480
The one I ignored?

1041
55:26.040 --> 55:28.060
He was probably devastated that...

1042
55:28.250 --> 55:29.810
things didn't go according to plan.

1043
55:29.810 --> 55:31.240
And do you know

1044
55:31.530 --> 55:33.200
where Mr. Sarm is?

1045
55:33.390 --> 55:34.990
He's probably somewhere nearby.

1046
55:34.990 --> 55:38.090
He's probably crying so hard that he could flood Pak Chong right now.

1047
55:39.190 --> 55:40.860
Do not wait around, Jam.

1048
55:41.000 --> 55:42.930
What should I do, Song?

1049
55:44.470 --> 55:46.280
Why don't you propose back to him?

1050
55:46.760 --> 55:48.200
If he asks

1051
55:48.200 --> 55:49.280
what you brought to propose with,

1052
55:49.510 --> 55:50.670
just say,

1053
55:50.670 --> 55:52.060
"This kiss."

1054
55:52.410 --> 55:53.260
Trust me.

1055
55:53.560 --> 55:54.460
Works every time.

1056
55:54.460 --> 55:55.910
Thank you, Mr. Song.

1057
56:00.880 --> 56:02.270
You've got this, Jam.

1058
56:02.860 --> 56:03.650
He loves me!

1059
56:08.210 --> 56:09.640
He loves me not!

1060
56:12.960 --> 56:13.660
He loves me!

1061
56:17.540 --> 56:18.460
He loves me not!

1062
56:18.630 --> 56:19.660
Mr. Sarm.

1063
56:20.490 --> 56:21.470
Little...

1064
56:21.730 --> 56:22.680
Mr. Sarm.

1065
56:25.210 --> 56:26.550
I am here to make it up to you...

1066
56:27.590 --> 56:28.730
Though I am late...

1067
56:29.260 --> 56:30.460
at least I am here.

1068
56:33.790 --> 56:35.550
Do not stay quiet, Mr. Sarm.

1069
56:35.680 --> 56:37.490
You are giving me bad vibes.

1070
56:38.230 --> 56:39.430
What did I tell you to call me?

1071
56:40.760 --> 56:41.810
Sarm.

1072
56:43.360 --> 56:44.080
Didn't catch that.

1073
56:45.030 --> 56:46.290
"Sarm."

1074
56:55.140 --> 56:56.290
Why are you here?

1075
56:57.730 --> 56:59.570
I am here to apply for a position.

1076
57:01.890 --> 57:02.860
You have to go there.

1077
57:02.860 --> 57:03.840
That's the headquarters.

1078
57:05.030 --> 57:06.160
Why did you come for me?

1079
57:08.040 --> 57:10.060
I can only apply for this position with you.

1080
57:11.390 --> 57:12.460
What position exactly?

1081
57:14.550 --> 57:16.320
It's...

1082
57:19.010 --> 57:20.860
The owner of Adisuan Farm's spouse.

1083
57:24.710 --> 57:25.690
I'm sorry, Little Jam?

1084
57:26.030 --> 57:27.240
Am I daydreaming?

1085
57:27.240 --> 57:28.290
I must be.

1086
57:29.720 --> 57:30.310
Little Jam.

1087
57:30.750 --> 57:31.320
Little Jam.

1088
57:31.790 --> 57:32.860
Slap me in the face.

1089
57:32.970 --> 57:33.910
Give me a wake-up slap.

1090
57:34.060 --> 57:35.070
This is impossible.

1091
57:35.260 --> 57:35.730
Little Jam.

1092
57:35.730 --> 57:37.270
Give me a slap. A slap, a slap...

1093
57:52.310 --> 57:53.530
Is this clear enough

1094
57:54.290 --> 57:55.330
that this is not a dream?

1095
57:57.810 --> 57:58.720
I'm almost awake now.

1096
58:07.660 --> 58:08.860
Is this clear enough?

1097
58:10.320 --> 58:11.120
Just a little more...

1098
58:11.260 --> 58:12.730
Is it clear now, Sarm?

1099
58:13.190 --> 58:14.290
Do not be so tense.

1100
58:15.160 --> 58:16.320
I am not.

1101
58:16.320 --> 58:17.260
I did it without knowing.

1102
58:17.450 --> 58:18.270
So...

1103
58:19.110 --> 58:20.010
You're making it up to me...

1104
58:20.330 --> 58:21.680
and you want to be my spouse?

1105
58:22.020 --> 58:22.610
Mm.

1106
58:24.170 --> 58:26.120
Do you accept?

1107
58:33.550 --> 58:34.290
If so...

1108
58:35.340 --> 58:37.150
show me what you've got.

1109
58:37.910 --> 58:39.040
I have none.

1110
58:40.170 --> 58:41.800
I always burn an omelet when I make one.

1111
58:44.860 --> 58:46.650
All I can make is cup noodles.

1112
58:51.710 --> 58:54.150
But I can buy you yogurt drinks.

1113
58:56.370 --> 58:57.130
And...

1114
58:57.930 --> 58:59.260
What do you want as your payment?

1115
59:01.490 --> 59:04.290
Love me and take care of me for the rest of your life.

1116
59:05.610 --> 59:08.010
Do not terminate this contract.

1117
59:11.260 --> 59:12.460
And what will I get in return,

1118
59:14.200 --> 59:14.860
hm?

1119
59:17.550 --> 59:20.080
I will take care of you as best as I can.

1120
59:29.260 --> 59:30.630
I'll give you headaches, you know?

1121
59:30.890 --> 59:31.890
Are you cool with that?

1122
59:32.860 --> 59:34.610
I have gotten used to it by now.

1123
59:35.390 --> 59:36.890
And what about me making a big deal out of everything?

1124
59:37.550 --> 59:38.440
I always do it.

1125
59:39.450 --> 59:41.050
You are my jam.

1126
59:41.520 --> 59:42.190
Oh...

1127
59:42.190 --> 59:42.870
It is true.

1128
59:43.430 --> 59:44.570
What about being this goofy?

1129
59:46.610 --> 59:47.530
Can you handle it?

1130
59:48.850 --> 59:50.640
No matter what you are like...

1131
59:51.010 --> 59:52.650
I will always love you.

1132
59:57.910 --> 59:59.710
So, do you accept me or not?

1133
01:00:01.970 --> 01:00:03.730
This position has always been yours.

1134
01:00:04.330 --> 01:00:05.470
You have no clue at all,

1135
01:00:05.930 --> 01:00:06.460
huh?

1136
01:00:07.660 --> 01:00:08.860
Let's get married.

1137
01:00:16.060 --> 01:00:16.930
Wait...

1138
01:00:17.120 --> 01:00:19.520
Aren't I supposed to say that?

1139
01:00:19.520 --> 01:00:20.170
And will you?

1140
01:00:20.170 --> 01:00:20.720
I will.

1141
01:00:20.860 --> 01:00:21.950
I will. I will.

1142
01:00:21.950 --> 01:00:22.330
Today.

1143
01:00:22.330 --> 01:00:22.830
Right now.

1144
01:00:22.830 --> 01:00:23.510
Right here.

1145
01:00:23.510 --> 01:00:23.890
Yes.

1146
01:00:24.030 --> 01:00:24.950
Right now.

1147
01:00:25.480 --> 01:00:26.410
Little Jam,

1148
01:00:26.410 --> 01:00:27.320
hold me, please.

1149
01:00:27.320 --> 01:00:28.060
I'm passing out.

1150
01:00:28.240 --> 01:00:28.870
Got an inhaler?

1151
01:00:28.870 --> 01:00:29.640
I have one.

1152
01:00:30.130 --> 01:00:31.370
Aside from the inhaler...

1153
01:00:33.030 --> 01:00:34.760
do you have my love in your backpack?

1154
01:00:36.330 --> 01:00:37.330
I do not

1155
01:00:39.770 --> 01:00:40.970
because...

1156
01:00:41.990 --> 01:00:43.660
your love

1157
01:00:46.280 --> 01:00:47.430
is right here.

1158
01:00:50.450 --> 01:00:51.470
I...

1159
01:00:51.680 --> 01:00:52.710
love...

1160
01:00:53.260 --> 01:00:54.460
you, Sarm.

1161
01:00:58.410 --> 01:00:59.540
Oh, Little Jam.

1162
01:00:59.600 --> 01:01:01.320
Stop being too adorable, can you?

1163
01:01:02.860 --> 01:01:04.800
I've run out of ways to show my love.

1164
01:01:04.990 --> 01:01:06.970
Do you think you are the only one falling in love?

1165
01:01:08.000 --> 01:01:10.870
I also love you very much.

1166
01:01:11.260 --> 01:01:12.910
But I'm still not your first.

1167
01:01:17.070 --> 01:01:18.690
You are neither my first

1168
01:01:20.190 --> 01:01:21.450
